---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 13</p>
  <h1>Jobs &amp; <em>workplaces</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Talk about work — the most common first question between adults. Name the <strong>job</strong> with <span class="ex">I'm a…</span> and the <strong>place</strong> with <span class="ex">I work at a…</span> Choose <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span> by the sound, and add <span class="ex">-s</span> for he and she: <span class="ex">She works at a hospital.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">a / an + job</span>
    <span class="tag">work at · in · as</span>
    <span class="tag">9 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read a short work introduction.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>a / an + job, and at / in a + place.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match jobs to places, choose, and build.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Talk about your job and a coworker's.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">We choose <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">an</span> by the <strong>first sound</strong>, not the spelling: <span class="ex">a nurse, a doctor, a manager</span> but <span class="ex">an engineer, an accountant, an electrician</span> — these start with a vowel sound.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="half past">half past</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quarter to">quarter to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Japan">Japan</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Japanese">Japanese</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>7:30 is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="half past" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> seven. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(previous lesson · telling the time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Emi is from Japan. She is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Japanese" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(older lesson · nationality)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The meeting starts <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> nine. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(common contrast · at + time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the jobs</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>People at work. Say each one aloud: <span class="ex">She’s a doctor. He’s a cook.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/doctor.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">doctor</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/teacher.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">teacher</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cook.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cook</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/police-officer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">police officer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/firefighter.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">firefighter</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/farmer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">farmer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mechanic.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mechanic</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/office-worker.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">office worker</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/scientist.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">scientist</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/artist.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">artist</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/pilot.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">pilot</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/construction-worker.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">construction worker</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/factory-worker.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">factory worker</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/programmer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">programmer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/singer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">singer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/astronaut.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">astronaut</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/judge.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">judge</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/student.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">student</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the workplaces</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Where people work. Say each one aloud: <span class="ex">She works at a hospital. He works in an office.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/office.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">office</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hospital.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hospital</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/school.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">school</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/factory.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">factory</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/store.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">store</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bank.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bank</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hotel.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hotel</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/house.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">home</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read about Marco at a party</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Hi, I'm Marco. I'm a nurse. I work at a hospital downtown. My wife is an engineer — she works for a big tech company. What do you do?"</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Marco says <span class="ex">a nurse</span> but <span class="ex">an engineer</span>. Say both aloud. What sound does <strong>engineer</strong> start with? Why is it <span class="ex">an</span>?</li>
      <li>Two patterns name work: one names the <strong>job</strong> (<span class="ex">I'm a nurse</span>) and one names the <strong>place</strong> (<span class="ex">I work at a hospital</span>). Which little word comes before the job? Which comes before the place?</li>
      <li>Marco's wife <span class="ex">works for a company</span>. Why is it <span class="ex">works</span> and not <span class="ex">work</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — read the job, then choose a or an</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Say the job aloud first. A vowel sound takes <b>an</b>; everything else takes <b>a</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I'm <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> nurse. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(starts with /n/)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>She's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> engineer. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(starts with /e/)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>He's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> accountant. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(starts with /a/)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I'm <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> manager. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(starts with /m/)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> electrician. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(starts with /e/)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: name the job, name the place</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>When someone asks <span class="ex">What do you do?</span>, you have two natural answers:</p>
  <p><strong>1. Name the job.</strong> &nbsp;<span class="ex">I'm a nurse.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class="ex">I work as a nurse.</span></p>
  <p><strong>2. Name the place.</strong> &nbsp;<span class="ex">I work at a hospital.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class="ex">I work in an office.</span></p>
  <p>For a company, use <span class="ex">for</span>: <span class="ex">She works for Toyota.</span></p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>job</th><th>typical workplace</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>teacher</b></td><td><b>school</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>nurse</b> · <b>doctor</b></td><td><b>hospital</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>chef</b> · <b>waiter</b></td><td><b>restaurant</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>accountant</b> · <b>manager</b> · <b>designer</b></td><td><b>office</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>receptionist</b></td><td><b>hotel</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>salesperson</b></td><td><b>store</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">shop</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>What is the difference between <span class="ex">as</span> and <span class="ex">at</span>? <strong>As</strong> introduces the <em>job</em>: <span class="ex">work as a chef</span>. <strong>At / in</strong> introduces the <em>place</em>: <span class="ex">work at a restaurant</span>.</li>
      <li>Do we say <span class="ex">I am nurse</span>? <strong>No.</strong> A job after <em>be</em> needs <span class="ex">a / an</span>: <span class="ex">I'm a nurse.</span></li>
      <li>What changes for <strong>he</strong> and <strong>she</strong>? The verb adds <span class="ex">-s</span>: <span class="ex">I work</span> → <span class="ex">She works</span>. After a teacher word like <em>teach</em>, we add <span class="ex">-es</span>: <span class="ex">He teaches.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the linking word</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The word after <span class="ex">work</span> depends on what comes next — a job, a place, or a company:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">work as a + JOB &nbsp; · &nbsp; work at / in a + PLACE &nbsp; · &nbsp; work for a + COMPANY</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1 — choose as, at, or for</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">A job follows <b>as</b>; a place follows <b>at</b>; a company name follows <b>for</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="as">as</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="for">for</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I work <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="as" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a chef. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(job: chef)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I work <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a restaurant. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(place: restaurant)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She works <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="for" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> Google. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(company: Google)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>He works <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="as" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a driver. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(job: driver)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>They work <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a bank. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(place: bank)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>My cousin works <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="for" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a small startup. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(company: a startup)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 2 — match each job to its workplace</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a job, then tap the place where that person usually works</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="nurse">nurse</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="chef">chef</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="teacher">teacher</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="accountant">accountant</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="receptionist">receptionist</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="nurse" data-placeholder="hospital">hospital</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="chef" data-placeholder="restaurant">restaurant</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="teacher" data-placeholder="school">school</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="accountant" data-placeholder="office">office</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="receptionist" data-placeholder="hotel">hotel</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i work as a nurse">
    <h3>Drill 3 — build the job sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Name your job with <span class="ex">as</span>. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="nurse">nurse</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="as">as</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="work">work</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she works at a hospital">
    <h3>Drill 4 — build the place sentence with -s</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Talk about her, not you. Remember the <span class="ex">-s</span> on the verb and <span class="ex">at</span> before the place.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="hospital">hospital</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="works">works</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="nurse" data-fix="I'm a nurse." data-why="A singular job after be needs an article. We say I'm a nurse, not I'm nurse.">
    <h3>Drill 5 — the missing word</h3>
    <p>Tap the word where something is missing in front of it.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i'm">I'm</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="nurse">nurse.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="work" data-fix="He works in an office." data-why="For he and she, the present verb adds -s. We say He works, not He work.">
    <h3>Drill 6 — fix the verb for he</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="he">He</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="work">work</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="in">in</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="an">an</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="office">office.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 — name the job, then say it</h3>
    <p>Read the cue and say <span class="ex">I'm a…</span> or <span class="ex">I'm an…</span> aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> your job: nurse &nbsp;→&nbsp; I'm…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I'm a nurse.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> your job: engineer &nbsp;→&nbsp; I'm…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I'm an engineer.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> your job: accountant &nbsp;→&nbsp; I'm…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I'm an accountant.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> your job: chef &nbsp;→&nbsp; I'm…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I'm a chef.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> your job: electrician &nbsp;→&nbsp; I'm…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I'm an electrician.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two busy people</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“My sister is a nurse at the city hospital. She starts early, at six. Her husband is a cook in an Italian restaurant. He works at night. They are both very busy, but they love their jobs.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood jobs in a real description.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="at the hospital">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Where does the nurse work?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the hospital">at the hospital</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at a restaurant">at a restaurant</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at a school">at a school</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a cook">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is her husband’s job?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a cook">a cook</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a nurse">a nurse</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a teacher">a teacher</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="at night">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. When does he work?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at night">at night</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at six in the morning">at six in the morning</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on weekends">on weekends</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>What do you do?</b> Answer about your real job — or a dream job — in two ways: name the job, then name the place. <span class="ex">I'm a designer. I work at a small studio.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A coworker or friend:</b> Describe someone you know using <span class="ex">he / she</span> and the <span class="ex">-s</span> ending. <span class="ex">My friend Ana is a doctor. She works at a hospital.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Where do people work?</b> The teacher names a job; you say the typical place in a full sentence. <span class="ex">A chef works in a restaurant. A receptionist works at a hotel.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Mingle at a party:</b> Role-play meeting three new people. Ask and answer. <span class="ex">What do you do? &nbsp;I'm an accountant. I work for a bank. And you?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Guess the job:</b> The teacher describes a workplace or a task; you guess the job. <span class="ex">"I work in a hospital and help patients." → "Are you a nurse?"</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the patterns back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To name my job I say <strong>I'm ___ a nurse</strong> or <strong>I work ___ a nurse</strong>. To name the place I say <strong>I work ___ a hospital</strong>. For a company I say <strong>I work ___ a company</strong>. I use <strong>an</strong> before a job that starts with a ______ sound.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about your own work and one about a coworker, using the <strong>-s</strong> ending correctly.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can name a job with a / an, match jobs to workplaces, and use work as, at, in, and for correctly.">
    <h3>Final quiz — jobs, places, and linking words</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="an">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. She's ___ engineer.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the">the</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. I'm ___ manager.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a">a</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an">an</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the">the</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="hospital">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. A nurse usually works at a ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="hospital">hospital</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="school">school</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="restaurant">restaurant</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="bank">bank</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="restaurant">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. A chef usually works in a ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="restaurant">restaurant</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="office">office</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="hotel">hotel</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="factory">factory</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="as">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. I work ___ a teacher.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="as">as</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at">at</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="for">for</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="at">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. He works ___ a hotel.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="as">as</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at">at</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="for">for</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She works at a bank.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She works at a bank.">She works at a bank.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She work at a bank.">She work at a bank.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She works at bank.">She works at bank.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I'm a doctor.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. Someone asks "What do you do?" Which answer is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I'm a doctor.">I'm a doctor.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I'm doctor.">I'm doctor.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I doctor.">I doctor.</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
